    "body": "The test still fails on Windows after PR #4287.\n\n- Host: bacon (Windows 11 NUC), quick gate of main at `9b141e1122fa` (the merge commit of PR #4287), 2026-11-27 04:17 UTC.\n- Test: `mcp_live` `idle_timeout::a_configured_finite_window_expires_on_the_listener`. The other 28 tests of the binary pass.\n- Panic at `crates\\app\\tests\\mcp_live\\idle_timeout.rs:72:44`:\n\n```\nclosed: Os { code: 10060, kind: TimedOut, message: \"A connection attempt failed because the connected party did not properly respond after a period of time, ...\" }\n```\n\nThe client gets the idle notice. Then the second `read_line` does not get end-of-file in 3 s. The listener does not close the connection on Windows after it sends the notice. A drop of one socket handle does not close the connection while a clone of the handle is open. An explicit `shutdown(Shutdown::Both)` after the notice can be necessary.\n\nThe run before the fix (02:47 UTC) failed at the same line.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
